Revision history for browser

0.41 2026-09-17
 - fix Browser::Runner::request leaking a launched browser process if launch() or newPage() itself failed (e.g. launch() started a real process, but the subsequent newPage() call then died) - those two calls previously ran before the eval block that guards playwright->quit() cleanup, so no cleanup was ever attempted; they now run inside it, matching the cleanup discipline already used for every other failure path in this method (D2B-047)

0.40 2026-09-17
 - add a test guarding .env's VERSION field against being malformed (e.g. a typo like "0.2O") or referring to a release never actually recorded in Changes; previously nothing caught either mistake (D2B-046)

0.39 2026-09-17
 - add explicit use_ok() calls for Browser::Search, Browser::Runner::NodeRuntime, and Browser::Runner::BrowserPath to t/00-load.t, which previously only exercised Browser::CLI and Browser::Runner directly (the other three loaded only transitively, so a real syntax error in any of them would not have been caught by this smoke test) (D2B-045)

0.38 2026-09-17
 - fix browser.search's --engines silently accepting a duplicate engine name (e.g. `--engines bing,bing`), which would retry the exact same walled engine a second time wasting a full request/browser-launch cycle; the requested engine list is now deduplicated (case-insensitively, preserving order of first occurrence) before use (D2B-044)

0.37 2026-09-17
 - fix package.json's version field violating SemVer (leading zero in "0.01.0"); changed to the valid "0.1.0". Low practical impact since the package is private and never published, but a real spec violation that could confuse strict tooling (D2B-043)

0.36 2026-09-17
 - fix browser.search's --engine/--engines matching engine names case-sensitively, so a capitalized or mixed-case value (e.g. `--engine Bing` or `--engines DuckDuckGo,BING`) died with "Unknown engine" even though the intent was unambiguous; both the requested name(s) and the known engine list are now compared case-insensitively (D2B-042)

0.35 2026-09-17
 - fix browser.search's --engines parsing dying with "Unknown engine" on a human-friendly comma-separated value with whitespace around the commas (e.g. `--engines "bing, google"`); each engine name is now trimmed of leading/trailing whitespace before being looked up (D2B-041)

0.34 2026-09-17
 - fix _skill_root's local-development cwd fallback, which trusted any current directory that merely had both a 'cli' and a 'lib' subdirectory (a coincidental match on an unrelated directory would silently resolve to the wrong skill root); it now also requires the skill-specific marker lib/Browser/CLI.pm to exist before trusting the cwd guess, falling through to the reliable __FILE__-relative resolution otherwise (D2B-038)

0.33 2026-09-17
 - fix _version_satisfies_spec silently mishandling npm version-spec syntax it doesn't understand (tilde ranges, comparison operators, space-separated ranges) by falling through to a plain string-equality check that is silently wrong for anything but an exact match; it now dies with a clear "Unsupported version spec" error for those cases while exact versions, '*', 'latest', and caret ranges keep working exactly as before (D2B-037)

0.32 2026-09-17
 - fix NODE_PATH growing an unbounded duplicate module-path entry every time _ensure_node_runtime is called in a long-lived process (e.g. a persistent dashboard rather than this skill's own one-shot CLI); it now dedupes the existing NODE_PATH before prepending the module path (D2B-035)

0.31 2026-09-17
 - remove an unreachable dead-code check in _browser_path_is_usable ('return 0 if $exit != 0' after _run_quiet_command, which only ever dies on failure or returns 0 on success and can never return any other nonzero value); added a clarifying comment explaining why only the eval/$@ check is needed (D2B-034)

0.30 2026-09-17
 - fix --ask/--askme silently no-opping when the confirmation read from stdin hits EOF (stdin closed, redirected from /dev/null, or already drained): it used to return undef immediately and the command proceeded as if the user had pressed Enter; it now dies with a clear "stdin is not interactive" error instead (D2B-031)

0.29 2026-09-17
 - fix browser.search never bounding each engine attempt with a timeout, relying solely on Playwright's own longer internal default; it now defaults to a 10 second per-engine timeout (overridable via the new --timeout-ms flag, matching browser.get/post/png's own flag), so a slow/unresponsive engine fails fast instead of stacking long waits across several default engines (D2B-040)

0.28 2026-09-16
 - fix the Node runtime auto-heal copy step, which shelled out to Unix `cp -R` (nonexistent on native Windows Perl), by replacing it with a portable Perl-native recursive copy that preserves symlinks (e.g. node_modules/.bin entries), empty directories, and file permission bits the same way `cp -R` did (D2B-036)

0.27 2026-09-16
 - refuse an unrecognized --browser value with a clear "Unsupported browser type" error naming the invalid value and the supported list (chrome, chromium, firefox, webkit), instead of letting a typo reach Playwright's own launch() and produce an opaque native error (D2B-033)

0.26 2026-09-16
 - fix _response_document's fragment-detection check, which accepted any opening tag paired with any closing tag (e.g. '<div>text</span>') as trustworthy HTML instead of escaping it into the safe fallback; now requires the tag names to actually match (case-insensitively) via a backreference (D2B-032)

0.25 2026-09-16
 - fix Runner::request's success-path cleanup: a playwright->quit() failure after a successful GET/POST/PNG no longer discards the already-computed result, matching the same eval-wrapped cleanup the error path already used (D2B-029)

0.24 2026-09-16
 - fix browser.search's all-engines-failed error, which blanket-attributed every engine failure to a CAPTCHA/bot-check wall even when the real cause was a request exception (network error, missing browser binary, timeout); the error now names each engine's real failure reason and only mentions --ask when a genuine CAPTCHA was actually encountered (D2B-039)

0.23 2026-09-16
 - fix browser.post's window.__BROWSER_POST__ JS assignment being built via unsafe raw concatenation of encode_json's byte-string output: normalized to a proper character string and escaped the Unicode LINE SEPARATOR/PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR characters, which are legal JS line terminators in source text and could otherwise let a POST response body break out of the intended JS string literal (D2B-030)

0.22 2026-09-16
 - fix browser.search launching a visible (non-headless) browser instead of headless - it never passed `headless` through to the runner, and an unset headless defaults to false; browser.get/post/png were unaffected since they always set it explicitly (D2B-028)

0.21 2026-09-16
 - fix browser.search's default duckduckgo engine URL, which pointed at duckduckgo.com/html/ - verified live to 302-redirect to html.duckduckgo.com/html/ - to build the request directly against html.duckduckgo.com, avoiding an unnecessary extra HTTP round trip on every duckduckgo search (D2B-027)

0.20 2026-09-16
 - add `dashboard browser.search <query>`: returns structured, ranked search results (rank/title/url/snippet), automatically falling back past any engine that comes back CAPTCHA/bot-walled instead of hand-picking an engine and hand-parsing HTML. Default engine order is bing, google, duckduckgo; `--engine`/`--engines` override the order, `--max` caps the result count, and an all-engines-walled query fails with a structured error naming the walled engines and pointing to `--ask` (D2B-026)

0.19 2026-09-16
 - fix `browser.get`/`browser.post`/`browser.png` wrongly refusing a URL argument of the literal string "0" as Missing URL, because the CLI's presence check used Perl truthiness instead of definedness/emptiness (D2B-025)

0.18 2026-09-16
 - stop reading and JSON-decoding the skill's own package.json up to 4 separate times within one stale-runtime check; it is now cached by path+mtime and read at most once per _node_runtime_is_current call (D2B-024)

0.17 2026-09-16
 - fix docs/usage.md's and README.md's Captcha Detection descriptions, which described a pre-D2B-009 detection shape and then, after a first pass, still overstated the real check as markup/widget validation instead of the plain 4-marker substring match `_is_captcha_page` actually does (D2B-020)
 - add the 4 docs/changes/*.md files (node-runtime-repair, browser-binary-validation, browser-png, mit-license) that already existed but were missing from README.md's Documentation index (D2B-020)

0.16 2026-09-15
 - fix `--browser firefox`/`--browser webkit` launching against a Chromium/Chrome executablePath (CHROMIUM_BIN or auto-detected) instead of Playwright's own firefox/webkit binary (D2B-003)
 - fix Node runtime dependency version checking to follow npm's caret-range rules for 0.x versions correctly, instead of only comparing the major version (D2B-004)
 - join NODE_PATH using the platform's own path-list separator instead of a hardcoded ':', so the Node runtime resolves correctly on Windows (D2B-005)
 - fix browser-binary PATH auto-detection to split on the platform separator and try a `.exe` suffix on Windows (D2B-006)
 - broaden `browser.post`'s HTML-fragment detection so a response body with no `<!doctype html>`/`<html>` wrapper (and no `text/html`/`application/xhtml+xml` content-type) is still recognised as HTML rather than escaped into a `<pre>` block (D2B-008)
 - narrow `is_captcha` detection to real reCAPTCHA/hCaptcha widget markup or a challenge-page title, instead of free substring matching across the whole rendered page text, which false-positived on ordinary content that merely mentions captchas (D2B-009)
 - hold an exclusive lock around the whole stale-check-and-install sequence for the shared `$HOME/node_modules` tree, so two concurrent browser-skill invocations can no longer race each other's clear+copy and corrupt it (D2B-010)
 - remove `_run_command`/`_run_in_dir`, two dead helpers with no call site anywhere in the skill (D2B-011)
 - make `browser.get`'s title lookup as defensive as `browser.post`'s already is, so a `title()` failure no longer aborts the whole GET request (D2B-012)
 - split lib/Browser/Runner.pm (718 lines) into Runner.pm (orchestration), Runner/NodeRuntime.pm (Node dependency install), and Runner/BrowserPath.pm (browser binary discovery/validation), each under 500 lines - no behaviour change (D2B-013)
 - strip Perl's own "at FILE line N." trailer from CLI error output, so ordinary usage errors no longer leak internal source paths and line numbers to the user (D2B-015)
 - fix the shared perl-test Docker image so it can actually launch a real Chromium browser: Ubuntu's apt "chromium" package is only a broken snap-wrapper stub with no functional browser behind it in a container, so the image now installs Playwright's own bundled Chromium at build time instead (D2B-014)
 - refuse `--data` on `browser.get`/`browser.png`, naming `browser.post` - it was previously accepted and silently ignored (D2B-016)
 - refuse `--wait-until`/`--timeout-ms` on `browser.post`, naming `browser.get`/`browser.png` - both were previously accepted and silently ignored (D2B-017)

0.15 2026-05-06
 - add an explicit MIT license to the `browser` skill
 - document the MIT license in the README

0.14 2026-04-24
 - reject relative PATH hits such as `bin/chrome` when selecting a browser binary for Playwright
 - validate configured and discovered browser binaries with a quiet launchability check before passing them as `executablePath`
 - add fallback candidate handling for common macOS app bundle browser locations without trusting broken wrappers

0.13 2026-04-24
 - add `dashboard browser.png` to capture a rendered page screenshot
 - support `--file` with automatic `.png` suffix normalization when the caller omitted it
 - default screenshot output to a random `/tmp/browser-*.png` path and print the saved file path after capture

0.12 2026-04-22
 - repair Node runtime self-healing so stale merged module trees do not leave `uuid` in an ESM-broken state for `playwright_server`
 - align runtime installation with DD's staged `npx` package.json install pattern and clear affected module directories before copying fresh installs into `$HOME/node_modules`
 - auto-detect a usable Chromium or Chrome binary from `PATH` when `CHROMIUM_BIN` is not set
 - verify the runtime fix through Docker, direct host CLI execution, and the latest DD source checkout

0.11 2026-04-22
 - add `--wait-until` so callers can choose `networkidle`, `load`, or `domcontentloaded`
 - remove unproven documentation examples and keep only verified examples in the README
 - update public-site examples so Amazon uses `--wait-until load` where appropriate

0.10 2026-04-22
 - add 20 Amazon-focused examples covering search, account, cart, and product-page patterns
 - add 20 X-focused examples covering logged-out shell inspection, login, post viewing, and multi-page flows
 - record the live DOM verification limitation for Amazon and the live logged-out shell alignment for X

0.09 2026-04-22
 - expand the README with explicit JavaScript versus Perl controller guidance
 - document when `--jquery` is useful and how to mix Perl control with page-side JavaScript
 - add a large example library covering one-page tasks, multi-page flows, normal cases, and edge cases

0.08 2026-04-22
 - change ask-mode initial navigation to use `load` instead of `networkidle`
 - disable the initial ask-mode timeout by default so slow login pages stay open for manual work
 - keep `--timeout-ms` as an explicit override for bounded waits

0.07 2026-04-22
 - add `--playwright`, `--agent`, and `--flow` as controller-mode aliases for full Perl-side Playwright flows
 - make `--ask` compatible with controller-mode flows so manual login or CAPTCHA work can continue into scripted navigation
 - update tests and docs for multi-page browser journeys from one starting URL

0.06 2026-04-22
 - add `--jquery` to inject the local jQuery runtime into the page before script evaluation
 - document that Playwright itself does not provide jQuery unless the page already loaded it
 - update tests and docs for jQuery-enabled scripts

0.05 2026-04-22
 - add `--ask` and `--askme` to browser.get for visible interactive takeover
 - wait for terminal confirmation before capturing the final page payload after captcha or login work
 - update tests and docs for interactive ask-mode

0.04 2026-04-22
 - add `content_type`, `body_text`, and `is_captcha` to browser responses
 - detect obvious CAPTCHA or bot-check pages in browser.get and browser.post payloads
 - update tests and docs for the richer response payload

0.03 2026-04-22
 - make browser.get return the rendered HTML body alongside URL, status, and title metadata
 - update tests and docs to match the browser.get payload contract

0.02 2026-04-21
 - add package.json for DD-managed Node dependency installation
 - align browser runtime bootstrap with DD package.json install behavior under $HOME
 - update tests and docs for the package.json dependency gate

0.01 2026-04-21
 - bootstrap the browser skill with Playwright-backed GET and POST CLI commands
 - add dependency files for nodejs and the Playwright Perl module
 - add Docker-tested coverage, documentation, and ticket records
